   <chapter title="Overview">
       <p><b>File:</b> <code>OtherTests/SupportTests/Open_API_Documentation_test.cy.ts</code></p>
        <p><b>Folder:</b> <code>OtherTests/SupportTests</code></p>
        <p><b>Description:</b> Validates that the RegTek+ API documentation page is accessible after logging out of the system.</p>
        <p><b>Priority:</b> Medium</p>
        <p><b>Owner:</b> QA Team</p>
        <p><b>Tags:</b> regression, API, documentation, authentication</p>
        <p><b>Dependencies:</b> Cypress environment variable `api_baseUrl`</p>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Test Suites">
        <chapter title="Opens API Documentation">
        </chapter>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Test Scenarios">
        <procedure title="successfully opens API Documentation" id="test-1">
            <p><b>Scenario:</b> Access API Documentation after Logout</p>
            <p>Logs out from the current session and navigates directly to the API documentation URL to confirm availability and expected content.</p>
            <p><b>Priority:</b> Medium</p>
            <step>1) Click user options and select "Logout". 2) Confirm logout action in the modal. 3) Visit the API documentation URL. 4) Verify that "RegTek+ API Documentation" and "Authentication" sections are visible.</step>
            <chapter title="Expected Results">
                <p>• The API documentation page opens successfully and displays both the documentation title and the Authentication section.</p>
            </chapter>
        </procedure>
    </chapter>

    <chapter title="Execution">
       <chapter title="Run Individual Test">
           <code-block lang="bash">
               npx cypress run --spec "OtherTests/SupportTests/Open_API_Documentation_test.cy.ts"
           </code-block>
       </chapter>
      
       <chapter title="Run in Interactive Mode">
           <code-block lang="bash">
               npx cypress open --spec "OtherTests/SupportTests/Open_API_Documentation_test.cy.ts"
           </code-block>
       </chapter>
   </chapter>

